{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.95,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["U6"],
      "pins": ["U6.2"],
      "nets": ["unconnected-(U6-EN-Pad2)"],
      "observed": "The EN pin of the TPS62933 buck regulator (U6 pin 2) is marked as no_connect and is not connected to any net.",
      "expected": "The EN pin should be tied to VIN (+24V) or to a UVLO resistor divider to enable the regulator.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"141\") (name \"unconnected-(U6-EN-Pad2)\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"U6\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"EN\") (pintype \"input+no_connect\")))"}
      ],
      "impact": "The 5V rail may never turn on, leaving the entire board without power.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "category": "other",
      "components": ["T7", "T1", "R19", "R26", "J4"],
      "pins": ["T7.1", "T1.1"],
      "nets": ["NET0038", "/NET0061"],
      "observed": "FLOAT_LOW (NET0038) drives the base of NPN T7 via R19. When FLOAT_LOW is high (normal water level), T7 turns on and pulls the main pump MOSFET T1 gate (/NET0061) low, disabling the pump. When FLOAT_LOW is low (water low), T7 turns off, allowing T1 to be driven on by IO10.",
      "expected": "The low-level float switch should cut off the main pump when water is low. Thus, when FLOAT_LOW is low, the pump should be disabled, not enabled.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "float-switch interlocks for low-level pump cutoff"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"79\") (name \"NET0038\") ... (node (ref \"R19\") (pin \"1\")) ... (node (ref \"M2\") (pin \"J1_7\") (pinfunction \"IO0/ADC0\")))"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"50\") (name \"/NET0061\") ... (node (ref \"T7\") (pin \"3\") (pinfunction \"C\")) (node (ref \"T1\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"G\")))"}
      ],
      "impact": "The main circulation pump will run when the water level is low, risking dry running and pump damage. It will be off when water level is normal.",
      "confidence": 0.9
    },
    {
      "category": "other",
      "components": ["C71"],
      "pins": ["C71.1", "C71.2"],
      "nets": ["NET0095", "+3V3"],
      "observed": "C71 (100n) is connected between the FLOAT_HIGH input (NET0095) and the +3V3 rail.",
      "expected": "A filter capacitor on a switch input should be connected to GND, not to a supply rail.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"84\") (name \"NET0095\") ... (node (ref \"C71\") (pin \"1\")))"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"1\") (name \"+3V3\") ... (node (ref \"C71\") (pin \"2\")))"}
      ],
      "impact": "Noise on the float switch input will be coupled onto the 3.3V supply, potentially causing false high-level readings and erratic ATO valve behavior.",
      "confidence": 0.7
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain multiple anomalies. The most critical is that the TPS62933 buck regulator's EN pin is left unconnected, which may prevent the 5V rail from powering up. Additionally, the low-level float switch interlock for the main pump is inverted, causing the pump to run when water is low instead of cutting off."
}

